# The Gilded Hour, an original orchestral concert waltz (a valse lente) in A-flat major
# by DeepSeek & SZ. Slow and bittersweet rather than ballroom: 88 BPM in 3/4, the low strings and
# the harp keeping the waltz pulse with a Viennese lilt, the strings singing theme A, the horns
# answering it, the flute taking the lighter theme B, a dark middle in F minor, a slow climb back,
# the theme in full with a soft wordless choir under its last phrase, and a coda that ritards onto
# a soft A-flat. 136 bars, about four and a half minutes.
#
# The harmony is written once below, one chord symbol a bar, and every part is derived from it: the
# cellos take each root, the pad holds an open root-fifth-octave, the harp rolls a triad or seventh
# on beats two and three, and the pizzicato plucks the same chord's third and fifth. The melodic
# long notes are chord tones, so the parts agree without the melody being flattened.
#
# Built by its own generator, tools/arranger/the-gilded-hour.mjs, from tools/arranger/lib.mjs:
# the form, the themes, the voicings, the figures, the velocities and the microtiming all live
# there. No oboe, no tubular bells; the glockenspiel is only a touch of colour, and the choir a
# single soft lift before the end.
#
# chords: Ab Ab Fm7 Fm7 Dbmaj7 Dbmaj7 Eb7 Eb7
# chords @9: Abmaj7 Fm7 Bbm7 Eb7 Abmaj7 Db6 Bbm7 Eb7 Abmaj7 Cm7 Dbmaj7 Eb Fm7 Bbm7 Eb7 Abmaj7
# chords @25: Abmaj7 Fm7 Bbm7 Eb7 Abmaj7 Db6 Bbm7 Eb7 Abmaj7 Cm7 Dbmaj7 Eb Fm7 Bbm7 Eb7 Abmaj7
# chords @41: Eb Eb Ab Ab Fm7 Bbm7 Eb7 Eb Db Ab Fm7 Bbm7 Db6 Eb7 Ab Ab Fm7 Bbm7 C7 C7
# chords @61: Fm Fm Bbm7 Bbm7 C7 C7 Fm Fm Dbmaj7 Dbmaj7 Gdim7 C7 Fm Bbm7 C7 C7
# chords @77: Fm Fm Bbm Bbm Db Db Eb Eb Fm Fm Bbm7 Bbm7 Eb7 Eb7 Eb7 Eb7
# chords @93: Abmaj7 Fm7 Bbm7 Eb7 Abmaj7 Db6 Bbm7 Eb7 Abmaj7 Cm7 Dbmaj7 Eb Fm7 Bbm7 Eb7 Abmaj7 Dbmaj7 Eb Fm7 Bbm7 Db6 Eb7 Ab Ab
# chords @117: Abmaj7 Db6 Abmaj7 Eb7 Fm7 Bbm7 Eb7 Abmaj7 Db6 Ab Dbmaj7 Eb Fm7 Bbm7 Eb7 Eb7 Abmaj7 Abmaj7 Db6 Abmaj7
#
# Form:
# 1-8: Intro: the pulse, the pad, the strings first call
# 9-24: A1: the strings state theme A
# 25-40: A2: theme A again, fuller, the horns answering
# 41-60: B: theme B on the flute, lighter
# 61-76: Middle: the waltz darkens in F minor
# 77-92: Build: a slow climb back to the major
# 93-116: A3: theme A in full, the whole orchestra
# 117-136: Coda: the waltz slows and says goodbye
#
